# Quarto build output
**/.quarto/
**/.paper-review/
**/_freeze/
**/_build/
# Quarto names its sidecar directory after the source file stem, so this has to
# match any stem, not just index (chapter files are named after their directory).
**/*_files/
**/index.html
# Part openers render to their own filename rather than index.html, so the rule
# above does not catch them and one `git add -A` commits a build artifact.
book/parts/*.html
book/contents/parts/*.html

**/site_libs/
**/*.quarto_ipynb*

# Assembled / rendered site output
/_site/
**/_site/

# Stray build artifacts (regenerated; not source)
/scratch/
/output/

# LaTeX scratch files
**/*.aux
**/*.bbl
**/*.bcf
**/*.blg
**/*.fdb_latexmk
**/*.fls
**/*.idx
**/*.ilg
**/*.ind
**/*.lof
**/*.lot
**/*.out
**/*.run.xml
**/*.synctex.gz
**/*.toc
**/*.log
**/DescriptionTexts.txt
**/._*xref.json

# Publisher/private reference material
**/publisher-guidelines/
**/publisher-materials/

# marimo's WASM export copies sibling project files into the bundle; the export
# script scrubs them, this is the second line of defence.
www/notebooks/**/CLAUDE.md
www/notebooks/**/AGENTS.md
www/notebooks/**/GEMINI.md
www/notebooks/**/CODEX.md
www/notebooks/**/.claude/
